VIUA-DB(1) "Viua VM PUT_VIUAVM_VERSION_HERE" "Viua VM Manual"

# NAME

viua-db - the Viua VM debugger

# SYNOPSIS

*viua db* _executable_ [_args_...]

# DESCRIPTION

Debug programs running on Viua VM.

# OPTIONS

include(common/tool-options.scdoc)

None.

# DEBUGGER COMMANDS

## Show commands

Show commands display information about run-time state of the program and the
debugger, as well the program's dynamic values eg, actors, stack backtraces,
frames, registers.

These commands are *read-only* and *never* affect the state of the debugger or
the program.
See *Alter commands* and *Execution commands* to learn how to affect the state
of the debugger and the prorgam.

*show frame* [_n_]
	Present information about _n_-th frame.
	Frame *0* is the bottom-most frame on the stack.

*show actor*
	Present currently selected actor.

*show breakpoints*
	List set breakpoints.

*backtrace*, *bt*
	Present a backtrace of the currently selected actor.

## Info commands

Info commands display information about static state of the program ie, anything
that can be known about the program without running it.

These commands are *read-only* and *never* affect the state of the program.

*info main*
	Present information about the main function of the _executable_.

*info functions*
	Present information about functions in the debugged program.

*info jumps*
	Present information about jumps in the debugged program.

## Execution commands

These commands control execution of the debugged program.

*actor new* _fn_
	Create a new actor using function _fn_.

*stepi* [_n_]
	Execute (step through) _n_ instructions.
	By default *stepi* command executes a single instruction.

*run*, *r*
	Run the program until it exits, or until a breakpoint is hit.

*continue*, *c*
	Continue running the program after a breakpoint has been hit, ignoring the
	breakpoint set at the current instruction.

## Alter commands

Alter state of the debugger or the program.

*frame* _n_++
*up* [_n_]++
*down* [_n_]
	Use *frame* to set the frame to inspect.
	Use *up* or *down* to move between frames on a stack.

*break* [_addr_], *b* [_addr_]
	Set a breakpoint at _addr_ (by default at the current position).

# EXIT STATUS

|[ 0
:< Successful program execution
|  1
:  Invalid input

# FILES

|[ _executable__
:< The executable to debug.

The linker opens its input files read-only.

